  ('36242f46-ea10-5205-8f12-0421a9c103c4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the author respond to the objection that friendly messages take too much time to write?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author agrees that deadlines make clear messages impossible and suggests that companies hire more writers instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"The author ignores the objection and moves on to describe the visual design features that make software look polished.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The author admits to having cut that corner too, then argues that the time saved is simply shifted onto users and support staff.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author dismisses the objection as an excuse and accuses developers of not caring about the people who use their programs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author admits to having cut that corner too, then argues that the time saved is simply shifted onto users and support staff.$q$, $q$"I understand; I have shipped my share of mystery codes" concedes the point, and "The cost does not disappear. It moves" answers it. The tone is sympathetic, not accusing, which keeps developers listening.$q$, 'draft', 'b47fab89-20d0-5a29-9d95-b3fde7b1f6f0')
