  ('7a406ae5-fffb-5885-9cf9-fb789fe6874d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-authors-purpose'), null, 'easy',
   $q$What is the author's main purpose in this introduction?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To revise the familiar account by showing that ordinary residents shaped how a shared time was adopted","is_correct":true},{"text":"To argue that the towns of the valley should return to keeping their own local solar time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"To explain the science of how the position of the sun determines the time of noon in each town","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To prove that the railway company made a serious mistake when it announced a single valley time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To revise the familiar account by showing that ordinary residents shaped how a shared time was adopted$q$, $q$The author calls the book "the story of a long conversation" involving councils, a watchmaker, and a schoolmistress, in place of a story about one company decision. The author never says the railway's decision was a mistake.$q$, 'draft', 'a10f0fdd-fb91-54a2-8706-60ff47a4f21d')
