   $q$Why does the author concede that "Almost every sentence in that version is true"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To admit that the author's own research has failed to find anything new about the valley's past","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"To suggest that historians should never question an account that is supported by facts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"To show fairness and make clear that the objection concerns emphasis rather than factual error","is_correct":true},{"text":"To criticize earlier historians for including too many true details in their accounts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show fairness and make clear that the objection concerns emphasis rather than factual error$q$, $q$Granting the facts makes the author sound careful, and it sharpens the real complaint: the tidy story leaves the towns out. The next paragraph presents new records, so the author has not failed to find anything new.$q$, 'draft', 'a10f0fdd-fb91-54a2-8706-60ff47a4f21d')
