   $q$How does the author treat the visitors who asked why the dead trees were not removed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author calls their question fair and answers it fully, treating them as reasonable people who can be persuaded.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author suggests they know little about nature and should leave decisions about the forest to trained experts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The author ignores their concern and focuses only on describing the wildlife that can be seen along the trail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The author agrees with their complaint and promises that the dead trees will be cleared away within the year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author calls their question fair and answers it fully, treating them as reasonable people who can be persuaded.$q$, $q$"The question is fair, and you deserve a full answer" sets a respectful tone that makes readers more open to the explanation. The sign never talks down to visitors, and it defends keeping the trees rather than promising to remove them.$q$, 'draft', 'cc97a657-c4a9-53ca-be12-656d8a1b34e2')
