  ('c175e63a-6b2e-530c-b5db-8476b8d8b837', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How do the sentences "In a garden, it would be. But this preserve is not a garden." advance the author's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They criticize visitors who keep gardens at home for wasting effort on plants that do not support wildlife.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They grant that tidiness is the right standard in some places, then argue that the preserve should be judged by a different one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They admit that the preserve has been neglected and suggest that it should be redesigned to look more like a garden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"They compare two kinds of soil to show that dead wood breaks down faster in gardens than in forests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They grant that tidiness is the right standard in some places, then argue that the preserve should be judged by a different one.$q$, $q$The author concedes that a dead tree in a garden would be neglect, then redefines the preserve as a place meant to "let a forest behave as a forest." The shift in standard is the core of the reply, not a criticism of home gardeners.$q$, 'draft', 'cc97a657-c4a9-53ca-be12-656d8a1b34e2')
