   $q$What is the author's main purpose in this essay?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To persuade viewers to learn foreign languages so they no longer need to read subtitles","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To explain the software used to place subtitles on the screen at the correct moment","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To complain that festival audiences do not praise subtitlers by name after each screening","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"To reveal the careful interpretive choices behind subtitles that most viewers never notice","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To reveal the careful interpretive choices behind subtitles that most viewers never notice$q$, $q$The author sets out to "describe what that forgetting hides," showing how every line requires choices about what to cut. The author calls being forgotten "a compliment," so the essay is not complaining about a lack of praise.$q$, 'draft', 'd8a9442f-b290-54dc-a716-2fe6a10d69f9')
