  ('73a64768-fcb1-50f1-816e-3e4327ee6f8f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the final paragraph reinforce the author's purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It apologizes for the mistakes in the author's subtitles and asks festival viewers to forgive any jokes that did not translate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It demands that viewers pay closer attention to subtitles than to images, reversing the advice given earlier in the essay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It makes a deliberately modest request and then reframes the film as partly written for the viewer, answering the opening idea of being forgotten.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It introduces new evidence about reading speeds to prove that most viewers cannot follow subtitles in a foreign film.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It makes a deliberately modest request and then reframes the film as partly written for the viewer, answering the opening idea of being forgotten.$q$, $q$"I am not asking you to watch the subtitles instead of the film" keeps the request small, and "also written for you" gives the hidden work meaning, echoing the opening claim that the author's job is "to be read and then forgotten." The author explicitly does not ask viewers to watch subtitles instead of images.$q$, 'draft', 'd8a9442f-b290-54dc-a716-2fe6a10d69f9')
