values
  ('8b9c0354-5dc0-5683-bc6f-cc205f02c3c1', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-authors-purpose'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which statement best expresses the author's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Stores should begin fining shoppers who leave carts in the parking lot, since that is the only way to change habits.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"Shopping cart corrals are placed too far from parking spaces, so stores are to blame for abandoned carts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Returning a shopping cart is a meaningful test of character precisely because nothing forces anyone to do it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"People who leave a shopping cart even once are careless and should feel ashamed of their selfish behavior.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Returning a shopping cart is a meaningful test of character precisely because nothing forces anyone to do it.$q$, $q$The author argues that returning the cart is "enforced by nothing at all," which is why it reveals character. The author says "I do not think anyone is a bad person for leaving a cart once," and never calls for fines.$q$, 'draft', 'f866cb3d-2962-5033-be6d-0a5486cd3d02')
