  ('ddea6ccd-4693-574d-b03f-d8a47b39dc48', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In the final line, the wet track reflects the speaker so that "there are two of us running." How does this image use the setting to resolve the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reflection shows Desmond still running beside the speaker after the handoff is complete.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The reflection pairs the speaker with a second self, suggesting the past failure now runs alongside, no longer in the way.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The reflection reminds the speaker that the rain has ruined the race and the times will not count.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The reflection reveals that the speaker is distracted by the water and is about to stumble.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The reflection pairs the speaker with a second self, suggesting the past failure now runs alongside, no longer in the way.$q$, $q$The rain that erased the chalk now produces a double image, turning the obstacle into a sign that the speaker's former self is joined rather than feared. Desmond has finished his leg, and the reflection is explicitly "my reflection."$q$, 'draft', '03e6d0f6-e71c-5fe6-899b-f266f515aef5')
