   $q$Why does the author save the coordinator's news about the other teams for the final section?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It turns Nadia's earlier warning about \"a hole\" in the shape into the actual outcome, so her choice to stay proves decisive.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains why the line on the graph dropped, which readers could not understand until then.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It shows that Joaquin was right to want to cancel, since clouds covered most of the state.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It reveals that the other teams were wrong to set up their equipment along the predicted path.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It turns Nadia's earlier warning about "a hole" in the shape into the actual outcome, so her choice to stay proves decisive.$q$, $q$Nadia said "If even one team gets clouds, the shape has a hole in it"; learning all the others were clouded out shows her persistence alone kept the record from being empty. Joaquin was not proven right, because staying produced the night's only measurement.$q$, 'draft', '12e195df-ecf2-5fac-bb69-36e63ae20eaa')
