   $q$Ayse splits shale "the way you might turn pages in a book you were not sure you liked." How does this comparison connect character and setting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Ayse would rather be reading a novel than working outdoors in the heat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It echoes the idea that the bands are chapters, showing her patient, uncertain reading of the rock.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It reveals that Ayse dislikes Ms. Halvorsen's assignment and plans to stop working soon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It suggests that the shale is too soft to split and keeps tearing apart like paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It echoes the idea that the bands are chapters, showing her patient, uncertain reading of the rock.$q$, $q$Ms. Halvorsen called the stripes "a different chapter," and the page comparison extends that image to Ayse's slow work through forty plates. She keeps going until she finds the leaf, so she does not quit.$q$, 'draft', '46712a2a-e724-56f6-ab07-0a50ff40c324')
