   $q$How does Yusuf's note "first year" relate to the poem's final image of fish returning "as if it had been called by name once more"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both suggest the return is a single lucky event that is unlikely ever to happen again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Yusuf's note shows he is disappointed by the small count, while the poem's image shows the river is overwhelmed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"Both suggest the fish are a brand-new species that has never lived in the river before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Both treat the return as a beginning with a future, though Yusuf looks ahead to years of counting while the poem looks back to an older memory being restored.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both treat the return as a beginning with a future, though Yusuf looks ahead to years of counting while the poem looks back to an older memory being restored.$q$, $q$"First year" implies more years will follow, and the poem calls the fish "a memory older than mills," so its return is a restoration. The poem's "once more" rules out the idea that the fish are new to the river.$q$, 'draft', 'f3773370-9e38-55ca-b9b8-ff228a411527')
