   $q$How is Duvall's chart related to Lindqvist's?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It replaced his chart entirely because factories had found his eight sizes too inaccurate for men.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It filled a gap in his chart, applying his method of measuring many people to a group that chart fit poorly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It was created at the army's request so that women serving as nurses could wear uniforms.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It copied his measurements but divided them into more sizes so tailors could do fewer alterations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-relationship"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It filled a gap in his chart, applying his method of measuring many people to a group that chart fit poorly.$q$, $q$Lindqvist's chart came from recording many recruits; Duvall did the same with "the women who came to her shop," a group his chart fit poorly. She measured new people rather than copying his records.$q$, 'draft', '808ede3a-4c5b-588c-9124-0ef5b93698a5')
