   $q$Based on the examples in paragraph 4, the word "trepidation" most nearly means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"nervous fear about something to come","is_correct":true},{"text":"tiredness from losing sleep","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"eager excitement about performing","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-connotation"},{"text":"careful rehearsal of each step","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$nervous fear about something to come$q$, $q$The examples (imagining her bow skidding, picturing the judges, a tightening stomach) all show fear about the audition. Lying awake is a result of her trepidation, not its meaning, so "tiredness from losing sleep" mixes up cause and effect.$q$, 'draft', 'aecd3af9-8e2c-5bb5-9588-8dfbb806fb29')
