   $q$Which phrase from the passage best helps the reader determine the meaning of "intransigent"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"writing them into formal regulations\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"\"persuading people to use it was another\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"\"They refused to give up the measures their grandparents had used\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"the advantages became hard to ignore\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"They refused to give up the measures their grandparents had used"$q$, $q$The phrase right after "intransigent" shows people refusing to give up their old measures, which defines the word as stubbornly unwilling to give in. The phrase about persuading people hints at resistance but does not show what that resistance looked like.$q$, 'draft', 'e37da047-2bee-568c-af25-28a37df398a5')
