values
  ('4eb5e3f0-94bd-599a-b157-b425fd8ab075', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-context-clues'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In paragraph 3, Teodor does "something audacious." Which meaning fits this context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"careless and done by accident","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"daring and willing to take a risk","is_correct":true},{"text":"cautious and purely defensive","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"rude and unfair to an opponent","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$daring and willing to take a risk$q$, $q$The move is called "an offer so bold" and later shown to be a deliberate plan, so audacious means daring. It cannot be an accident, because the gambit is something a player does "deliberately."$q$, 'draft', 'd3f73304-a08e-58b6-95d5-044d1fa76b4a')
