   $q$In paragraph 3, the author calls the slime mold "this humble organism." Which meaning of "humble" fits this context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"small in total number","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"poor and struggling to find food","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"simple and ordinary in nature","is_correct":true},{"text":"modest about its own achievements","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$simple and ordinary in nature$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 stresses that the organism has no brain and a basic body, and "Yet" sets that simplicity against its surprising abilities, so humble means simple and ordinary. "Modest about its achievements" is a real meaning, but it describes a person's attitude, which a slime mold cannot have.$q$, 'draft', 'fecbe175-7fa7-5b78-9537-bfdb8012095e')
