   $q$What can most reasonably be inferred about why mosquito counts fell after the first two summers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Regular tidal flow and the arrival of fish made the pools a poorer place for mosquitoes to breed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The conservation board began spraying the pools once residents complained about the insects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The sunken areas filled with sediment so quickly that the pools disappeared within a year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The cordgrass grew tall enough to shade the pools and keep mosquitoes from laying eggs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Regular tidal flow and the arrival of fish made the pools a poorer place for mosquitoes to breed.$q$, $q$Counts rose when pools were "stagnant" and fell "after the tide began to reach those pools twice a day and small fish moved in," which points to flushing and fish. Spraying and shading are never mentioned, so those choices add causes the text does not give.$q$, 'draft', '3ff382a5-a9f8-573d-b837-4003a3af3d49')
