   $q$According to the passage, why does the university draw water from deep in Lake Orrin?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The deep water is cleaner and will not damage the computing equipment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The bottom layer stays at about four degrees Celsius throughout the year.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The surface water is reserved for the people who fish and swim there.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A deep intake is required so that warm water can return near the shore.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bottom layer stays at about four degrees Celsius throughout the year.$q$, $q$The second paragraph explains that the bottom layer "stays at about four degrees Celsius all year, even when the surface warms in summer." The lake water never touches the equipment at all, so cleanliness is not the stated reason.$q$, 'draft', '5d129fe6-6231-5d60-be2c-59bb5eb7dcc5')
