   $q$The river was "so still that it looked as if someone had ironed it." What does this comparison show about the water?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Someone had cleaned trash out of it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It was flowing quickly toward the dock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It was warm enough to give off steam.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Its surface was perfectly smooth and flat.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its surface was perfectly smooth and flat.$q$, $q$Ironing removes wrinkles, so the comparison stresses a surface without ripples, which matches "so still." Nothing about ironing here suggests heat or steam.$q$, 'draft', '82ef284f-3030-5958-9564-1bbb52a0a775')
