   $q$The coach tells Tomas, "you are winning a race against your own crew." What does she mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"His extra effort is out of rhythm with the crew and works against them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Tomas is the fastest rower and should be moved to a better boat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The crew has been trying to slow Tomas down on purpose.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Tomas has been secretly racing other team members after practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His extra effort is out of rhythm with the crew and works against them.$q$, $q$The coach follows up by telling him to "give it less, at the same moment as everyone else," so his problem is pulling out of sync with his teammates. The remark is a criticism, not praise suggesting he deserves a better boat.$q$, 'draft', '82ef284f-3030-5958-9564-1bbb52a0a775')
