   $q$The grandfather has "the polite calm of a man who had been translated many times before." What does describing him as "translated" suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He is used to relying on interpreters and patiently waits for them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He has been moved to many different cities by his employer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-in-context"},{"text":"He has written several books that were published in Spanish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He is annoyed that Lucia translates his words so slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He is used to relying on interpreters and patiently waits for them.$q$, $q$Applying "translated" to a person rather than words shows that being spoken for is a familiar experience to him, which explains his "polite calm." Calm is the opposite of annoyance, so the irritated reading conflicts with the text.$q$, 'draft', '86b331d4-0106-5eee-abe8-a5909b2a91ff')
