   $q$The grandfather says, "A bridge is not the only way across a river. Sometimes the best help is a better boat." What does he mean in context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ms. Haddad should have spoken more slowly so Lucia could keep up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They should take a different route home that avoids the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"A translator is not the only way to communicate; a drawing also works.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Lucia should stop translating because she is not very good at it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A translator is not the only way to communicate; a drawing also works.$q$, $q$Lucia called herself "the bridge," and the drawing was the "better boat" that carried the meaning across without her. He adds "You will learn the words," so he is encouraging her, not telling her to quit.$q$, 'draft', '86b331d4-0106-5eee-abe8-a5909b2a91ff')
