   $q$Why does the author describe the Premium Plan last among the three boiling plans?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The list saves the plan with the most technical detail for those who keep reading.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The list ends with the best plan because the author wants readers to buy it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-author-speaker"},{"text":"The list builds to its most absurd point, that owners must pay extra to boil water on weekends.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The list moves from most expensive to least expensive so owners can compare prices easily.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The list builds to its most absurd point, that owners must pay extra to boil water on weekends.$q$, $q$Each plan is sillier than the last, and the climax is paying a monthly fee for weekend boiling, a basic function. The speaker may want sales, but the author is mocking that goal, not endorsing it.$q$, 'draft', '4ea542ed-e248-5aee-8d85-3b5eaf814e77')
