   $q$The mentor "never wrote that it was sad." What does this detail suggest about how she recorded the melting ice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She was told by her supervisors that emotional words were not permitted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She did not notice the ice was shrinking because she focused only on numbers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She believed the melting ice was a good sign for the valley below it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She let plain measurements carry the meaning rather than stating her feelings.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She let plain measurements carry the meaning rather than stating her feelings.$q$, $q$The stanza says she "trusted numbers" to "speak more plainly than a sign," so her silence is a choice, not ignorance. Nothing mentions supervisors or rules.$q$, 'draft', '3ec31ea2-aa88-543c-afa9-4ea25ff7b8e2')
