  ('8f905305-c5ea-5013-9406-bfde6e75011c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In the sixth stanza, the speaker does "not write the word I'd say." What is the effect of this understatement?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By refusing to name the feeling, the speaker shows that the ice loss does not matter much.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"By refusing to name the feeling, the speaker criticizes the mentor's careless note taking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"By refusing to name the feeling, the speaker makes the reader sense its weight more strongly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By refusing to name the feeling, the speaker admits to forgetting the right scientific term.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By refusing to name the feeling, the speaker makes the reader sense its weight more strongly.$q$, $q$The withheld word invites readers to supply the grief themselves, so the restraint intensifies emotion. The careful repetition of the mentor's method shows respect, not criticism.$q$, 'draft', '3ec31ea2-aa88-543c-afa9-4ea25ff7b8e2')
