  ('06dcea5c-57a0-51fe-94ac-c15bc7d14428', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The last stanza repeats the opening but ends with a plan to "drive another soon, / and count, and write it down." How does this altered return contribute to the poem's meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It suggests the ice will soon return, so the poem ends on a note of scientific triumph.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It suggests a cycle with no comforting resolution: the work continues because the loss continues.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests the mentor will come back to lead the work, so the poem ends where it began.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It suggests the speaker will give up the survey, so the poem ends with a clear break.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It suggests a cycle with no comforting resolution: the work continues because the loss continues.$q$, $q$The near repetition traps the poem in a loop, and the added plan to measure again implies the ice will keep retreating. Nothing points to the ice returning or the work stopping.$q$, 'draft', '3ec31ea2-aa88-543c-afa9-4ea25ff7b8e2')
