-- Passage rg12-literary-structure-pov-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('fa642568-bf70-5126-804d-ecbee9e0b069', 'rg12-literary-structure-pov-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Minor Setback at the Regatta$q$, $q$The Harwell Rowing Club would like to thank everyone who attended Saturday's regatta and to offer a brief account of our performance, which several spectators have described as memorable.

Our crew of eight left the dock at 9:40 in excellent spirits. Coach Oyelaran had reminded us that rowing is a sport of rhythm, and for the first two hundred meters our rhythm was very consistent, in that each of us maintained a different one throughout.

At the halfway mark, a small amount of river entered the boat. Our coxswain, Priya Venkataraman, calmly informed us of this development. She informed us again at the six hundred meter mark, somewhat less calmly, and a third time when the water had reached our ankles.

We would like to stress that at no point did the crew stop rowing. We continued with determination as the boat sat lower and lower in the water, until it became clear that we were no longer rowing so much as wading in a seated position.

The race officials were extremely gracious. They sent a launch to collect us, along with our oars, our water bottles, and one of Tomas's shoes, which had chosen to continue the race independently.

We did not finish first. In the interest of accuracy, we did not finish. However, the club is pleased to report that our crew was the only one to be photographed by the local newspaper, and the only one to receive a standing ovation from the riverbank.

Repairs to the hull are underway. Practice resumes Tuesday at dawn.$q$, 'draft')
