   $q$What does the narrator mean by saying the crew's rhythm "was very consistent, in that each of us maintained a different one"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rowers were practicing a new method in which each person rows alone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The rowers were perfectly together, just as the coach had asked them to be.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"The rowers each chose a rhythm that matched the speed of the river current.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The rowers were completely out of sync, though the sentence begins as if praising them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rowers were completely out of sync, though the sentence begins as if praising them.$q$, $q$The sentence starts like praise, then reveals that each rower kept a separate rhythm, meaning no teamwork at all. Reading it as real coordination misses the turn at "in that."$q$, 'draft', 'fa642568-bf70-5126-804d-ecbee9e0b069')
