  ('1c36f83a-6fd5-5e23-90f1-9504dba98918', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The fable ends with the repaired bell ringing "exactly on time" while most people look at the sparrow. How does this ending shape the fable's meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the merchants returning to the tower, so the sparrow's role in the story is erased.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It gives the tower back its accuracy but not its importance, so its pride is answered with gentle comic irony.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It restores the tower's place at the center of town, so the fable rewards its patience.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"},{"text":"It punishes the tower by having it break again, so the fable closes with a tragic warning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It gives the tower back its accuracy but not its importance, so its pride is answered with gentle comic irony.$q$, $q$The clock is fixed and correct, yet attention has shifted to the bird, so the tower gets what it claimed to value (accuracy) and loses what it really wanted (respect). The resolution is comic, not tragic, since nothing breaks again.$q$, 'draft', '82995920-1dae-53b5-b0f3-13fc0535d6a7')
