   $q$The narrator says the comet's fixed position shows "remarkable patience." How does this explanation reveal the narrator's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator carefully tests the theory against the evidence and admits it might be wrong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"The narrator jokes about the comet because of already knowing it is only a smudge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-irony"},{"text":"The narrator bends an obvious warning sign into praise out of a strong wish for the discovery to be real.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator uses a scientific term that astronomers apply to comets that move slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator bends an obvious warning sign into praise out of a strong wish for the discovery to be real.$q$, $q$A comet that stays fixed against a porch railing is a clue to a lens problem, but the narrator turns it into a compliment. The later entries show the narrator is sincere, not joking.$q$, 'draft', '292d4398-3385-5e97-9236-fc0ae5fd6afc')
