   $q$The narrator says the observatories' silence means they "do not want to raise my hopes." What does this reveal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator is losing faith in the discovery and preparing for disappointment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"The narrator suspects the observatories have stolen the idea and named the comet themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The narrator understands how observatories work and correctly predicts their response.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"The narrator reads every sign as good news, which marks an unreliable narrator.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator reads every sign as good news, which marks an unreliable narrator.$q$, $q$Silence is a weak sign of interest, yet the narrator reads it as proof of importance, a pattern throughout the journal. The narrator shows no doubt, so losing faith does not fit.$q$, 'draft', '292d4398-3385-5e97-9236-fc0ae5fd6afc')
