-- Passage rg12-literary-structure-pov-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('17f4d92d-1a54-5d2c-9ec9-97ba34d2b3c2', 'rg12-literary-structure-pov-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Metronome$q$, $q$I have kept the time for forty years
in a room where the curtains fade,
and I have heard each student's fears
in every scale they played.

I do not hurry. I do not slow.
I am a pendulum, nothing more.
The girl who sits here doesn't know
her father practiced here before.

He played this sonata, page by page,
his fingers stumbling on the turn;
he was about her present age,
and just as stubborn, just as stern.

He quit one winter, closed the lid,
and left the music on the stand.
I kept the beat. That's all I did.
I do not need to understand.

The years went by in quarter notes,
in other children, other hands;
I counted through their winter coats,
their spring recitals, summer plans.

And then this autumn she arrived,
her father's chin, her father's frown;
she sat, and sighed, and then she tried,
and set the old sonata down.

Tonight she finds his penciled marks:
a circled bar, a careful "slow."
She frowns and plays it through the dark,
and stumbles where he stumbled, so.

I do not hurry. I do not slow.
I only click, and click, and click.
She tries the turn again, and oh,
I must have lost count. That was quick.$q$, 'draft')
