   $q$The note in the tube says, "Thought someone should have it." How does this casual line work in light of the rest of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Its offhand tone understates the map's importance, which the story then reveals through Eliza's history.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Its offhand tone mocks the archive, which the story then criticizes for losing the map long ago.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"Its offhand tone hides the sender's identity, which the story then reveals to be Eliza Brandt herself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Its offhand tone shows that the map is worthless, which the story then confirms through Dr. Mahoe's research.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its offhand tone understates the map's importance, which the story then reveals through Eliza's history.$q$, $q$The sender treats the map as an attic curiosity, but the story shows it holds an unfinished survey and a forgotten surveyor, so the line is ironic in hindsight. Eliza worked in 1871, so she could not have mailed the tube.$q$, 'draft', 'a240e601-b238-5151-b51a-ef6370d26827')
