   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Strong coastal winds make fog collection impossible, so villages should rely on trucks and barrels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Fog nets collect water when tiny droplets strike plastic threads, merge into drops, and run into a gutter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Fog nets have now replaced truck deliveries and solved the water problems of every dry coastal town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"By patiently refining a simple mesh design, Alto Seco turned frequent fog into a useful, though limited, water supply.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By patiently refining a simple mesh design, Alto Seco turned frequent fog into a useful, though limited, water supply.$q$, $q$The passage traces the village from no way to use fog, through failures and adjustments, to a dependable but limited supply. The choice about droplets striking plastic threads describes only the mechanism in paragraph 2, not the passage as a whole.$q$, 'draft', '725e12f5-6347-5846-a7d8-5b61e97b87ea')
