   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A coastal village tried fog nets, but strong winds tore them in the first winter. Because the yield drops in late summer, the village decided that trucks remain its only reliable source.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-outcome"},{"text":"A dry coastal village began catching fog with mesh panels. After early failures, design changes made the nets productive enough for drinking water and a greenhouse, though they depend on weather and upkeep.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A dry coastal village built a brilliant system of fog nets that every desert town should copy. The engineer's clever design proves that technology can solve any shortage if people work hard enough.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"A coastal village stretched plastic mesh between poles on a ridge facing the sea. Fog droplets collide with the threads, merge into drops, and run down into a gutter that leads to a tank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A dry coastal village began catching fog with mesh panels. After early failures, design changes made the nets productive enough for drinking water and a greenhouse, though they depend on weather and upkeep.$q$, $q$The summary that mentions early failures and design changes covers the problem, the adjustments, the results and the limits without judgment. The summary calling the system "brilliant" adds praise and a claim the passage never makes.$q$, 'draft', '725e12f5-6347-5846-a7d8-5b61e97b87ea')
