   $q$What is the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Clocks in the eastern port of Calder ran several minutes ahead of clocks in the western town of Fenwick.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Railway travel in Merrow was dangerous because the company's trains frequently collided on single tracks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The railway's need for coordinated schedules led Merrow to replace local sun time with one shared standard time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Newspapers in Merrow successfully defended local sun time against the demands of the railway company.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The railway's need for coordinated schedules led Merrow to replace local sun time with one shared standard time.$q$, $q$Each paragraph follows the move from sun time to railway time and then to legal standard time. The difference between Calder and Fenwick is one example used to explain the starting situation.$q$, 'draft', '1bd1fd44-46a0-568c-8fbe-05daf0e93544')
