   $q$Which statement best captures the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Planting shade trees is the only effective way for a city to lower its summer temperatures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Reflective roof coatings are too costly and inconvenient for cities to use, so Corvana abandoned them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Corvana's test showed that reflective roofs reduce heat in useful ways but work best as one part of a broader cooling plan.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Dark asphalt shingles and tar absorb most of the sunlight that strikes them and release it as heat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Corvana's test showed that reflective roofs reduce heat in useful ways but work best as one part of a broader cooling plan.$q$, $q$The passage explains the problem, describes the test, weighs results and trade-offs, and ends with coatings as "one part of a wider effort." The choice about asphalt shingles and tar is only the opening explanation.$q$, 'draft', 'ee2e4caa-0d30-50c9-82b9-b7a35382e5a5')
