   $q$How do the third and fourth paragraphs work together to develop the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both paragraphs list benefits, which shows the coatings had no meaningful disadvantages.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The third presents the planners' opinion, and the fourth presents the residents' opposing opinion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The third describes the study's method, and the fourth reports its single main result.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The third reports the benefits of the coatings, and the fourth presents costs, which together support a measured conclusion.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The third reports the benefits of the coatings, and the fourth presents costs, which together support a measured conclusion.$q$, $q$Paragraph 3 opens "The results were striking" and lists gains, while paragraph 4 opens "The study also revealed trade-offs." Together they lead to the balanced conclusion in paragraph 5.$q$, 'draft', 'ee2e4caa-0d30-50c9-82b9-b7a35382e5a5')
