   $q$What is the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Underwater speakers can fully restore damaged coral reefs without any other kind of help.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Playing recordings of healthy reefs can draw young fish to damaged reefs and help start recovery, though it is no cure.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Warm water and storms have permanently destroyed most of the coral reefs near Pelandra.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Healthy coral reefs are noisy because shrimp snap their claws and fish grunt and chatter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Playing recordings of healthy reefs can draw young fish to damaged reefs and help start recovery, though it is no cure.$q$, $q$The passage builds from why sound matters, to the experiment, to results and limits, ending with sound as "a head start rather than a cure." The noisy reef detail only sets up the idea.$q$, 'draft', '13695ebd-8121-5451-b622-b5bdb0533b5f')
