   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Wheelchair basketball has become less exciting because modern chairs make the game too easy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Darius Okafor was the greatest wheelchair basketball player in the history of Larkmoor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Early basketball chairs had tall backs, large handles and wheels set straight up and down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Wheelchair basketball chairs improved through cooperation between athletes and builders, and those improvements reshaped the sport.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Wheelchair basketball chairs improved through cooperation between athletes and builders, and those improvements reshaped the sport.$q$, $q$The passage traces how player feedback led to design changes and how those changes transformed play, as the final sentence states. The description of tall backs, large handles and straight wheels is only a detail from paragraph 1.$q$, 'draft', '466576c1-bad1-576d-8384-9b3c0b9d2894')
