   $q$What is the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Old cylinder recordings are too faint and scratchy to be worth the cost of preserving.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Needles remain the safest and most reliable way to play old wax cylinder recordings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Scanning wax cylinders with light lets archives recover fragile old recordings without damaging them further.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Wax cylinders were used more than a century ago, before flat records became common.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Scanning wax cylinders with light lets archives recover fragile old recordings without damaging them further.$q$, $q$The passage moves from the problem of decaying cylinders to the light scanning method, its results and its costs, concluding that it preserves sound "without causing the very damage that playback once did." The first fact is only background.$q$, 'draft', 'b7112449-849e-5ec4-9e62-f4682a0e6017')
