   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author agrees with the council that benches cost too much, but suggests building a few new ones far from the main street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The author reports that store owners in Merrin Falls said customers stayed longer after the town added seating along its shopping street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The author argues that Ashgrove should restore its removed benches, citing benefits for walkers, local stores and community life, and suggests ways to reduce their cost.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author shows that Ashgrove's council foolishly destroyed its main street, and that only selfish officials would care more about paint than about their own neighbors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author argues that Ashgrove should restore its removed benches, citing benefits for walkers, local stores and community life, and suggests ways to reduce their cost.$q$, $q$An objective summary of an argument reports the author's claim and reasons without adding new judgments, as the summary citing benefits for walkers, local stores and community life does. The summary saying the council "foolishly destroyed" the street and calling officials "selfish" inserts harsh opinions the author never expresses.$q$, 'draft', '5f4b1c1d-67b8-5933-a5df-269b0018f69d')
