   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Recorded lectures are more effective for learning than lectures delivered in person.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Laptops should be banned from all lectures because handwriting always leads to better learning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Students who type their notes write longer notes than students who write their notes by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Notes help learning most when students process ideas in their own words, whether they write by hand or type.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Notes help learning most when students process ideas in their own words, whether they write by hand or type.$q$, $q$The passage moves from the first study to Valborg's follow-up and concludes that "the important difference is not between paper and keyboard but between copying and thinking." Paragraph 5 says banning laptops may not be necessary.$q$, 'draft', 'd249cb97-0a2d-5b50-85a8-e9c10880ce29')
