  ('cbe98ea3-74fb-55b6-8d36-ff196ca22337', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Research shows that typing is now the best way to take notes, since typists who summarize score higher than any students who write by hand on paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-finding"},{"text":"A follow-up study gave some typists an instruction to summarize the lecture in their own words. Those students wrote shorter notes, and their scores rose to nearly match the handwriting group.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"One study found handwritten notes led to better understanding than typed notes, possibly because handwriting forces rephrasing. A follow-up found typists who summarized in their own words did nearly as well, suggesting method matters more than tool.","is_correct":true},{"text":"One study found handwritten notes led to better understanding than typed notes. This proves that laptops harm learning, and schools that still allow them are making a serious mistake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-later-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One study found handwritten notes led to better understanding than typed notes, possibly because handwriting forces rephrasing. A follow-up found typists who summarized in their own words did nearly as well, suggesting method matters more than tool.$q$, $q$The summary ending "method matters more than tool" covers both studies and the conclusion without judgment. The summary claiming "laptops harm learning" stops at the first study and adds an opinion that the passage's later evidence contradicts.$q$, 'draft', 'd249cb97-0a2d-5b50-85a8-e9c10880ce29')
